I don’t have a built‑in “list files” command, so I’ll need a file that contains the names of the files you’re interested in.  
If you can create a text file that lists all the files in the directory (for example, by running `ls > filelist.txt` in your shell), I can then use `grep` to pull out the ones that contain “test” in their name.

Once you have that file ready, let me know the name of the file (e.g., `filelist.txt`) and I’ll run:

```json
{
  "name": "grep",
  "arguments": {
    "file_name": "<your_file_list>",
    "pattern": "test"
  }
}
```

That will return the lines that match, i.e., the file names that include “test”.
